  #line-at(72pt, 345.12pt, "*Correspondence: ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#467886"))
  #line-at(162.24pt, 345.12pt, "sid.assa@sydney.edu.au")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(72pt, 380.76pt, "Abstract: ")
  #line-at(72pt, 416.28pt, "Control of thermal emission is important in a number of applications from thermal energy ")
  #line-at(72pt, 443.88pt, "harvesting and management and sensing of gas and chemical to thermal camouflage.")
  #line-at(72pt, 471.48pt, "Semiconductor-based devices can be engineered to enable electrical control of thermal ")
  #line-at(72pt, 499.08pt, "emission, offering high modulation speed and ease of voltage control. Existing device designs ")
  #line-at(72pt, 526.68pt, "for modulating thermal emission rely on semiconductors other than silicon, such as III-V and ")
  #line-at(72pt, 554.28pt, "II-VI compounds, which are expensive. The silicon platform offers several advantages, ")
  #line-at(72pt, 581.88pt, "including significantly lower cost, CMOS compatibility, and mature fabrication processes. ")
  #line-at(72pt, 609.48pt, "However, a silicon-based design for modulating thermal emission remains absent. Here, we ")
  #line-at(72pt, 637.08pt, "present an all-silicon device utilising electrical control over carrier dynamics to modulate a ")
  #line-at(72pt, 664.68pt, "narrowband thermal emission in the mid-infrared region. We design a silicon device ")
  #line-at(72pt, 692.28pt, "exhibiting voltage-controlled narrowband thermal emission at 10 µm and confirm its ")
  #line-at(72pt, 719.88pt, "performance using electromagnetic calculations. This work paves the way for scalable, low-")
  #line-at(72pt, 747.48pt, "cost, and integrated thermal emission devices made possible by the silicon platform. ")
]

