#original-page(595.32pt, 841.92pt, none)[
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(72pt, 83.16pt, "emission can be found in ref.")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 8.04pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(211.2pt, 78.6pt, "41")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(219.36pt, 83.16pt, ". The architecture comprises a top photonic crystal slab, ")
  #line-at(72pt, 110.76pt, "separated by an air gap from a silicon p-n junction, with a perfect electric conductor (PEC) ")
  #line-at(72pt, 138.36pt, "acting as a back reflector. This structure supports guided resonance modes that couple to free-")
  #line-at(72pt, 165.96pt, "space radiation from above the top surface of the photonic crystal. The operation of the ")
  #line-at(72pt, 193.56pt, "device proceeds as follows: The carriers in p-n junction generates thermal emission, which ")
  #line-at(72pt, 221.16pt, "can be controlled by the applied voltage bias. This emission couples into the guided ")
  #line-at(72pt, 248.76pt, "resonance mode within the plane of the device. The air gap serves dual purposes: it provides ")
  #line-at(72pt, 276.36pt, "electrical isolation between the p-n junction and the photonic crystal, and it enables tuning of ")
  #line-at(72pt, 303.96pt, "the device's optical response. The top photonic crystal facilitates coupling between the guided ")
  #line-at(72pt, 331.56pt, "modes and free-space radiation by periodically scattering the guided modes, which propagate ")
  #line-at(72pt, 359.16pt, "along the slab plane, out to free space. This external coupling is most effective under a phase-")
  #line-at(72pt, 386.76pt, "matching condition, where the propagation constant of the guided mode matches with the ")
  #line-at(72pt, 414.36pt, "periodicity of the photonic crystal, establishing a guided resonance")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 8.04pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(392.76pt, 409.8pt, "42")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(400.92pt, 414.36pt, ". The outcoupling of ")
  #line-at(72pt, 441.96pt, "thermal emission via guided resonance modes results in narrowband thermal emission at a ")
  #line-at(72pt, 469.56pt, "wavelength determined by the periodicity and geometry of the photonic crystal. ")
  #line-at(72pt, 505.08pt, "Achieving unity absorptivity and emissivity at the guided resonant wavelength also requires a ")
  #line-at(72pt, 532.68pt, "balance between the rate at which the guided resonance modes are thermally generated and ")
  #line-at(72pt, 560.28pt, "the external coupling rate at which they outcouple to free space. The internal generation rate ")
  #line-at(72pt, 587.88pt, "of these modes depends on the carrier concentration within the p-n junction and its spatial ")
  #line-at(72pt, 615.48pt, "distribution relative to the mode’s electromagnetic field profile. Under this critical coupling ")
  #line-at(72pt, 643.08pt, "condition, the device realises unity peak absorptivity and emissivity at the resonant ")
  #line-at(72pt, 670.68pt, "wavelength, as shown in ref.")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 8.04pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(209.16pt, 666.12pt, "41")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(217.32pt, 670.68pt, ". ")
  #line-at(72pt, 706.32pt, "Applying a negative voltage bias to the p-n junction depletes the carriers in the junction (Fig. ")
  #line-at(72pt, 733.92pt, "2b), thereby reducing the internal generation rate. This occurs because the depletion region ")
  #line-at(72pt, 761.52pt, "expands, diminishing the number of free carriers available to interact with the ")
]

