  #line-at(72pt, 83.16pt, "silicon as a promising platform for modulating mid-infrared thermal radiation through carrier ")
  #line-at(72pt, 110.76pt, "dynamics. Here, we discuss potential improvements and design considerations to enhance the ")
  #line-at(72pt, 138.36pt, "device’s performance. ")
  #line-at(72pt, 174pt, "Our device exhibits a narrowband thermal emission at a centre wavelength of 10 µm. This ")
  #line-at(72pt, 201.6pt, "centre wavelength is a consequence of the periodicity of the photonic crystal structure, which ")
  #line-at(72pt, 229.2pt, "can be engineered to achieve the desired emission wavelength. Unlike designs that rely on ")
  #line-at(72pt, 256.8pt, "material-specific resonance, this approach allows for far greater flexibility in tuning the ")
  #line-at(72pt, 284.4pt, "thermal wavelength across a wide range. The tunability of this design is particularly ")
  #line-at(72pt, 312pt, "advantageous for applications requiring spectral control, such as spectroscopy and sensing. ")
  #line-at(72pt, 347.52pt, "The narrowband thermal emission of 2 nm can be advantageous for applications requiring ")
  #line-at(72pt, 375.12pt, "high spectral selectivity, such as spectroscopy. The device design inherently allows tuning of ")
  #line-at(72pt, 402.72pt, "the linewidth to meet application-specific requirements. For instance, we can broaden the ")
  #line-at(72pt, 430.32pt, "linewidth of our device by increasing the doping concentration in both the p- and n-regions of ")
  #line-at(72pt, 457.92pt, "the p-n junction, thereby increasing thermal emission from carriers, together with a ")
  #line-at(72pt, 485.52pt, "corresponding increase in the grating depth to maintain critical coupling condition. ")
  #line-at(72pt, 513.12pt, "Conversely, reducing doping with the corresponding reduction in grating depth narrows the ")
  #line-at(72pt, 540.72pt, "linewidth. ")
  #line-at(72pt, 576.36pt, "The polarisation selectivity of our device, which emits narrowband thermal radiation only in ")
  #line-at(72pt, 603.96pt, "the TM polarisation, is a consequence of the design of the top one-dimensional grating. This ")
  #line-at(72pt, 631.56pt, "grating supports only TM-polarised guided resonance at 10 µm. This polarisation selectivity ")
  #line-at(72pt, 659.16pt, "could be beneficial in polarisation-sensitive sensing applications.  For polarisation-insensitive ")
  #line-at(72pt, 686.76pt, "design, one can design a two-dimensional (2D) photonic crystal slab that, by symmetry, ")
  #line-at(72pt, 714.36pt, "support both TM and TE polarisations at the same wavelength, enabling thermal emission in ")
  #line-at(72pt, 741.96pt, "both polarisations. ")
]

// arXiv source page 13
#original-page(595.32pt, 841.92pt, none)[
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(72pt, 83.16pt, "The angular dependence of our device’s thermal emission is also consequence of the photonic ")
  #line-at(72pt, 110.76pt, "crystal design, specifically the dispersion of the guided mode near the grating wavevector. ")
  #line-at(72pt, 138.36pt, "This angular could be useful for applications requiring directional or steerable thermal ")
  #line-at(72pt, 165.96pt, "emission, such as directional sources with angularly modulated output. When angular ")
  #line-at(72pt, 193.56pt, "independence is desired, the dispersion of the guided mode can be made flat by designing a ")
  #line-at(72pt, 221.16pt, "2D photonic crystal with a flat band structure, as demonstrated in ref.")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 8.04pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(404.88pt, 216.6pt, "46")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(413.04pt, 221.16pt, ". This eliminates the ")
  #line-at(72pt, 248.76pt, "angular dependence of the guided resonance frequency, allowing the device to emit ")
  #line-at(72pt, 276.36pt, "uniformly in all directions. ")
  #line-at(72pt, 312pt, "Our design relies on a floating photonic crystal slab above a p-n junction to provide electrical ")
  #line-at(72pt, 339.48pt, "isolation as well as for tuning the emissivity response. Such a structure can be achieved by a ")
  #line-at(72pt, 367.08pt, "MEM system")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 8.04pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(137.04pt, 362.52pt, "47")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(145.08pt, 367.08pt, ", where the slab is supported by flexible anchors to enable precise control over ")
  #line-at(72pt, 394.68pt, "the slab’s position, or by putting support elsewhere")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 8.04pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(317.28pt, 390.12pt, "48")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(325.44pt, 394.68pt, ". ")
  #line-at(72pt, 430.32pt, "Finally, silicon")
  #line-at(146.28pt, 430.32pt, "device designs that enable electrical control of thermal emission in silicon can ")
  #line-at(72pt, 457.92pt, "be extended beyond the specific p-n junction realisation demonstrated here. Other silicon-")
  #line-at(72pt, 485.52pt, "based structures could offer advantages. For example, a design based on a metal-oxide-")
  #line-at(72pt, 513.12pt, "semiconductor (MOS) capacitor, which provides similar voltage control over carrier ")
  #line-at(72pt, 540.72pt, "concentration, can be engineered to achieve voltage-controlled dynamic thermal emission. ")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "bold", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(72pt, 576.36pt, "Conclusion")
  #set text(font: "Times New Roman", size: 12pt, weight: "regular", style: "normal", fill: rgb("#000000"))
  #line-at(72pt, 611.88pt, "We have presented an all-silicon device design that enables voltage control of thermal ")
  #line-at(72pt, 639.48pt, "emission. The design integrates the thermal emission from carriers in a silicon p–n junction, ")
  #line-at(72pt, 667.08pt, "whose quantity can be controlled by an applied voltage, with a photonic crystal to generate ")
  #line-at(72pt, 694.68pt, "polarised, narrowband thermal emission in the mid-infrared region. The use of silicon offers ")
  #line-at(72pt, 722.28pt, "great benefits in terms of cost-effectiveness, scalability, matured and established fabrication ")
  #line-at(72pt, 749.88pt, "processes, and seamless integration with CMOS technology. This work opens new avenues ")
]

